course: dictionary
lesson: 8224
title: Words that show deep respect
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Revere is a verb, and it means to respect and admire someone or something very deeply. Context helps you find that meaning. In history and religion lessons, people revere saints, leaders and holy places. The phrases «deeply revered» and «revered as a hero» show that revered is a strong, positive word.
explain: Watch for the capital letter. «Paul Revere rode in 1775» uses Revere as a name, not a verb. Paul Revere was an American who rode at night to warn that British soldiers were coming. So if Revere has a capital letter and is a person's name, it is not the verb.
explain: Try the swap check. «Christians revere God and the saints» becomes «Christians respect and admire God and the saints very deeply». That still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Try the same check with any sentence where you meet revere.
fact: Revere means to respect and admire someone or something very deeply.
fact: The forms are revere, reveres, revered and revering. Revered is the past form.
fact: «Paul Revere» is a person's name, with capital letters. Its clue is the capital R.
fact: Paul Revere is reported to have warned that «the Regulars are coming out», meaning the British army soldiers.
fact: The famous line «The British are coming!» comes mostly from a poem written in 1860, not from the ride itself.
exercise: «Many people revere the saints in history and religion lessons.» What does revere mean? | Ignore completely | Feel scared of | Draw a picture of | *Respect and admire very deeply
exercise: Fill the gap: Christians ___ God and the saints. | Laugh at | Argue with | *Revere | Forget
exercise: In «The British are coming!», where does this famous line mostly come from? | A letter from Paul Revere himself | A history book from 1775 | A news report from the night of the ride | *A poem written in 1860
test: Which word means nearly the same as revere? | *Admire | Argue | Ignore | Forget
test: «The villagers ___ the old healer as a hero.» Which word fits the gap? | Ignored | Feared | *Revered | Drew
exam: Revere is a verb. Which word is its past form? | Revere | *Revered | Revering | Reveres
